Z||000000||v8vinnie||01-16-2001||07:42 PM||||i was just woundering if the engine movement with all that torque will up set the rear end,it seems to get squirlly under full throttle,and some times i hear a bag, like as if the trans going up and down. i have the archie kit in there and the front of the engine is solidly mounted. question is does the movement of the engine and trans effect the syspension movement causing this?. i already put in poly cradle bushings and lower control arm polybushings , what do you guys think,im going to get the poly trans mounts, would this help?||||reg||11
Z||000001||v8vinnie||01-17-2001||07:14 AM||||dont tell me you guys are stumped on this one,i was woundering if it could also be the stock 60 series tires?. im going to try max air pressure and see if that helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jimmy||01-17-2001||12:38 PM||||   Poly trans mounts may help.  I noticed that when I put my Archie kit together there was not much clearance between the cradle and the adapter plate(starter side).  This was because my trans mounts were shot.  Bought new ones and it made a big difference.  <BR>   You could always wrap some paper around the cradle were the adapter sits above.  Then put some sort of chalk on the adapter plate, go out and drive around the block, make it bang, then see if thats were your problem is by looking at the paper for chalk marks.  Just an idea, hope everything works out.<P>Jim<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8<BR>87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||v8vinnie||01-17-2001||07:25 PM||||thanks ,i ordered the poly trans mounts and while i was talking to the salesmen? ,he said since i lowered my car you could install the rear strut upper brackets upside down and this will give you more travel before you hit the bump stops. did any of you guys do that,i should get the new mounts next week and let any one know the results!!||||reg||1
